speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, there have been the usual discussions with the House Leaders of the other two Parties and I think you will find unanimous consent for the adoption of the following motion with respect to the order of business for tomorrow:
That, notwithstanding any Standing or Special Order of this House, at 3.30 o'clock p.m. on Thursday, December 18, 1986, proceedings then before the House shall be interrupted and the House shall proceed to the consideration of Private Members' Business as scheduled on that day's Notice Paper;
Provided, that in relation to the proceedings to be interrupted at 3.30 o'clock p.m., the provisions of Standing Order 11 shall apply;
That at 4.30 o'clock p.m., on that day, the House shall revert to Statements by Ministers for the purpose of the presentation of a statement by the Minister of State (Finance), and the replies thereto;
Provided, that the Minister shall lay upon the table a document in relation thereto;
That provisions of Standing Order 19(6), in relation to the extension of that day's sitting, shall not apply; and
That, immediately upon the conclusion of proceedings in relation to this statement by the Minister, Mr. Speaker shall adjourn the House until the next sitting day.
